There IS documentation for netmud (aka TinyMUD).  It is contained in the
Library north of the Temple-- all of which is part of the "small.db" universe.

As the README file indicates, all you need to do to get started is:

% netmud <database> <dumpfile> [<port>]

The <database> contains the universe to use. 
The <dumpfile> will contain the universe with any changes made to it after
  3600 seconds elapsed time, or if the wizard (game manager) dumps the file
  manually.
The <port> is an optional port to connect the netmud server to.  The default
  is 4201, but you can use any port not already in use (check your /etc/services
  file to find out what ports are in use.)

To access the game, use telnet or some other client program to connect to the
  desired port:

% telnet <netmudhost> <port>

The <netmudhost> is the hostname of the machine you started netmud on.
The <port> is the portnumber netmud is listening on (default is 4201, as shown
  above.)



To access the documentation:
1. create a character using the command: create <charactername> <password>
2. go north using the command: go north (or just 'n').
3. go north again into the temple
4. go north again into the library
5. select the section of the documentation that you want: 1 = referance, 
   2 = construction costs, and other sillyness, 3 = administration commands
   You can enter the rooms containing the info by using the numbers, or the
   room name.     
6. Once you find the "book" (the command reference) that you want to read, just
   do so by: read <book>
   For example, If I am running the character "Me" and I am in the Library lobby,
   I can get info on the "Help" command by doing the following:

   reference   [to enter the reference room]
   oxford      [to select the OED of commands. Notice abbreviation is allowed.]
   read help   [to read the help section]


I must admit, it takes a bit getting use to, but it is rather interesting in that
you mush PLAY the game to learn how to play the game.  



